## Guidelines

1. Describe only what you can see. Do not guess what is said, who someone is, or what happens outside this frame.
2. Do not describe the camera (framing, lens, lighting) and do not mention that this is a frame.
3. If the frame shows almost nothing — a blank slide, a dark screen — say so plainly instead of inventing detail.

